# Spec 023 AC-7/AC-8, automatic (spec 013): the door run — Y in level 1 starts each level 24 px left of its door and
# runs right, so ten doors change level through an iris closing on the player (both screens) and reopening on the
# new level's start; the verdict is 60 Hz over the run. Then one more door by hand, with a screenshot mid-iris.
# PC:      nnh run platformer --pc --script examples/platformer/tests/doors.nnhs
# Console: nnh run platformer --script examples/platformer/tests/doors.nnhs   (Homebrew Launcher open, press Y)
fail-on "] E "
fail-on "60 Hz FAIL"

wait 30
tap Y
expect "doors: started" 10
expect "doors: 1 level1 -> bonus frame" 300
expect "doors: 2 bonus -> level1 frame" 300
expect "doors: 3 level1 -> bonus frame" 300
expect "doors: 4 bonus -> level1 frame" 300
expect "doors: 5 level1 -> bonus frame" 300
expect "doors: 6 bonus -> level1 frame" 300
expect "doors: 7 level1 -> bonus frame" 300
expect "doors: 8 bonus -> level1 frame" 300
expect "doors: 9 level1 -> bonus frame" 300
expect "doors: 10 bonus -> level1 frame" 300
expect "doors: done 10 irises" 300
wait 3

# The player stands left of level 1's door: walk in and catch the iris closing on it (both screens).
press RIGHT
wait 42
screenshot door-iris
release RIGHT
wait 120
end
